# Ludi Live

## Rules engine

Import `@ludi/rules` unchanged. Never edit `packages/rules` or `docs/GAME_RULES.md` for Ludi Live work.

## Authority

The server is authoritative. The overlay only renders server state.

## Adapters

Adapters only map chat to commands (`!join`, `!roll`, `!move 1-4`, `!stay`, `!leave`). The core never imports platform code.

## Gifts

Gifts are cosmetic only. They never affect dice, turns, seats, outcomes, or prizes (UK lottery law and TikTok rules). Keep the test that proves this.

## Canvas

The canvas is 1080x1920. The safe zone is x 100-980 and y 40-1380, taken from one screenshot and still to be confirmed on a real stream.

## Town colours

- Kingston `#E4202E`
- Ocho Rios `#0FAE47`
- Montego Bay `#FED100`
- Negril `#26272B`
- Border `#D9DCE1`

## UI

The UI matches the approved Wonder artboards exactly. Do not write UI code without Dean's approved mockup. The Waiting badge reads `WINNER CAN STAY`.

## Secrets

No secrets in the repo.

## Stack

Use one WebSocket stack (socket.io), one test runner (vitest), and one validator (zod via `@ludi/protocol`).

`tiktok-live-connector` is pinned to 2.4.0 (the last MIT release; later versions are AGPL) unless Dean decides otherwise.

## Proof

Prove each step with verify-ludi and green CI. Never merge or deploy without Dean.
